# SENTINEL AI — frontend production build environment
#
# IMPORTANT: do not commit a real API origin here.
#
# `VITE_API_BASE_URL` is a BUILD-TIME, PUBLIC value. Vite inlines it verbatim
# into the browser bundle, so it can never hold a secret, and changing it
# requires a rebuild — not just a restart.
#
# Supply the value from the hosting provider's build environment instead
# (Vercel: Project Settings -> Environment Variables -> Production), so one
# repository can serve staging and production. `frontend/vercel.json` refers to
# the project variable `vite_api_base_url`.
#
# The value must be scheme + host only, with no path, because the client
# appends the `/api/...` prefix itself:
#
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://<backend-origin>
#
# This file previously contained the placeholder
# `https://your-render-backend-url.onrender.com`. Vite compiled that literal
# into every production bundle, so the built app called a host that does not
# exist while `npm run build` still exited 0. A placeholder assignment is
# intentionally absent now and the build fails if one is reintroduced.
#
# Guard: frontend/scripts/validate-api-base-url.mjs
# Docs: docs/deployment.md (section "Frontend build & API origin contract")
